  "result": "Comparing the Drizzle schema (`src/server/db/schema/*.ts`) against every \"Indexes\" table in `docs/db/*.md`, two entries contradict the schema:\n\n1. **`docs/db/tables-issues.md`** — the `issues` table's index table lists `issues_project_number_idx` as covering `org_id, number`. The schema declares it as `uniqueIndex(\"issues_project_number_idx\").on(table.projectId, table.number)` (`src/server/db/schema/issues.ts:39`) — i.e. `project_id, number`, not `org_id, number`. (The doc's own \"Invariants\" section below even correctly says the uniqueness is \"within `(project_id, number)`\", directly contradicting its own index table row.)\n\n2. **`docs/db/tables-webhooks-search-and-infra.md`** — the `search_index` table's index list includes `search_index_org_updated_idx` on `org_id, updated_at`. The schema (`src/server/db/schema/webhooks.ts`) only declares one index on `search_index`: `index(\"search_index_org_kind_idx\").on(table.orgId, table.subjectKind)`. There is no `search_index_org_updated_idx`, and the table doesn't even have an `updated_at` column (it has `indexed_at`).\n\nANSWER: docs/db/tables-issues.md, docs/db/tables-webhooks-search-and-infra.md",
